                  <provenance type="#bs"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_432">Oxford, Oxfordshire.
                        Gloucester College; cell of Gloucester. </orgName><p>New College 49 is
                        evidently a present from John Whethamstede, abbot of St Albans, like London,
                        Bodleian ad Worcester Coll. MSS.: like them it is identifiable in
                        Whethamstede's booklist in London, BL, Arundel 34 (see under St Albans): see
                        D. R. Howlett and R. W. Hunt, BLR 10 (1982), pp. 225--28.</p><p>Identifiable
                        by the 'lamb and flag' and 'eagle' medallions in the border on fol. 1r with
                        the copy made for John Whethamstede, no. 9 in the list, 'Factura librorum de
                        compo[s]icione aliorum', 'Item in factura Petri Iohannis super Matheum lxs'
                        (Annales, p. 268); cf. Eton 103, Bodleian Auct. F. inf. 1.1, Cotton Nero
                        C.vi.</p><p>Chain staple on lower cover at foot; cf. the marks on Worcester
                        Coll. 233 (the distance from the first to the last of the four nails is
                        unusually long, c.115--1[..] in both MSS.).</p><p>II bands (cf. Worcester
                        Coll.).</p><p>Hand of fols. 14r--40v, 57v--159r is that of Worcester Coll.,
                        233. See D. R. Howlett &amp; R. W. Hunt, BLR 10 (1981), p.
                     225.</p></provenance>
               </history>
